{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112102,"nonce":"ikvrU496Lvwe3eH6Dxhr89ub8Uc=","title":"3.5 Dialog + interaction verbs","message":"Wave 3 — hands. Depends: 1.1, 2.4 (interactions observer). The modal\nstate-machine issue.\n\n## Goal\nDialogs and interactions, headless: letters answered, trades transacted,\ncomms used — without ever driving a UI widget. Plus the guarantee that the\nagent can always SEE what's awaiting input and always dismiss safely.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Action model (transact the model, not the UI)\n- decompiled: ChoiceLetter + LetterStack, Dialog_NodeTree/DiaNode (comms,\n  some quests), TradeDeal/Tradeable/TradeSession + Dialog_Trade (reference\n  only — the deal object is the API), ICommunicable, quest letters\n- MP's trade/caravan sync (existence proof + which mutations must be paired)\n\n## Scope\n- `letter list/read/choose {letter} {option}/dismiss` — options by label or\n  index, exactly as 2.4 reports them.\n- `comms {console} call {target}` + resulting node-tree navigation\n  (`dialog choose {option}`) — generic DiaNode walker so faction calls and\n  modded trees work uniformly.\n- `trade start {trader}` → session summary (tradeables, prices, silver both\n  sides) → `trade set {thing} {count}` (+ gift toggle) → `trade confirm`\n  (validates via TradeDeal.TryExecute) / `trade cancel`.\n- Unknown modded dialogs: appear in 2.4 interactions as opaque {type, title,\n  buttons}; `dialog dismiss` must always work (esc-equivalent).\n\n## Invariants\nZero UI-widget driving; every interaction reachable headless or visibly\nopaque+dismissible; trades atomic (confirm executes the whole deal or\nnothing, with the game's own validation errors surfaced).\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nTrade session lifecycle vs pause (sessions are windows in vanilla — own the\nlifecycle without the window); which comms actions matter v1 (visitor/trader\nrequests for Guests testing outrank military aid); quest accept flow coverage\nbeyond choice letters.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Dev-spawned trader: buy 10 meals + sell 5 shirts sight-unseen via verbs;\n  silver and stock verified correct after confirm; cancel leaves state\n  untouched.\n- Choice letter (quest offer) accepted via verb → quest active.\n- A modded/unknown dialog shows opaque in interactions and dismisses cleanly.","files":null}]}